# App. None of these are NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed, and that is the point: Next
# inlines any NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable into the browser bundle at build time, so
# the prefix is what decides whether a value can reach a client, not how the
# value is used. The publishable key is safe to expose and still does not need
# to be — nothing in this app runs Supabase from the browser.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Admin-only, for `npm run invite`. These go in a separate .env.admin
# (gitignored), NOT in .env.local and NEVER in Vercel: the secret key bypasses
# row-level security. SUPABASE_URL is the same project URL as above — it is
# repeated because .env.admin is loaded on its own, by that script only.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
# INVITE_BASE_URL=https://news.h72labs.com
